The attached image (Fig. 11) illustrates the difference in residual inflammation at injection sites two weeks after immunization with either aluminum hydroxide (AH) adjuvant or Nano-11 adjuvant. The left panel (AH) shows extensive granulomatous inflammation (*) with dense cellular aggregates in the skeletal muscle (M). In contrast, the right panel (Nano-11) exhibits significantly less inflammation (*), characterized by relatively few macrophages arranged in slender cords within the connective tissue between muscle fibers (M), indicating that Nano-11 causes a more transient and quickly resolving inflammatory response compared to AH.